messages:   18%|#7        | 105/600 [05:37<05:53,  1.40it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nObligatory alternative action refers to a situation in which the actor has committed an illegal act and caused the result, but the result cannot be avoided even if he abides by the law.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the following is an optional act of obligation?\n# Options:\nA) When a was driving normally, a pedestrian named wang rushed to a from the sidewalk and wang was injured\nB) B drunk driving, pedestrian wang also drunk, from the sidewalk suddenly rushed to b, wang was injured\nC) C driving speeding, pedestrian wang across the road, c too late to brake, wang hit\nD) D overload driving, pedestrian wang across the road, fortunately, ding emergency brake, did not hit wang', '<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to understand the definition of an "obligatory alternative action" and then apply it to each option to determine which one fits the criteria.\n\n1.**Definition Recap**:.\n   - An obligatory alternative action occurs when the actor has committed an illegal act and caused a result, but the result cannot be avoided even if the actor abides by the law.\n\n2.**Option Analysis**:.The pedestrian named Wang did not rush to the road illegally; rather, it was a driving recklessly that caused Wang\'s injury. This situation does not meet the criteria for a necessary alternative action.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
