messages:   25%|##5       | 152/600 [10:54<19:55,  2.67s/it][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nNearly all employees of the factory who have completed their high school diploma have earned their factory safety certificate, having easily completed the eight week training course. The high school graduates who haven' t earned the certificate are ones who have evening obligations that have prevented them from taking the course. Overall, though, most of the factory workers have not earned the certificate.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, if the statements above are true, which one of the following also must be true?\n# Options:\nA) A large proportion of the factory workers have not graduated from high school.\nB) A large proportion of students with high school diplomas have evening obligations that have prevented them from taking the eight week training course.\nC) Most of the workers who have earned the certificate are high school graduates.\nD) No factory worker without a high school diploma has completed the course and earned the certificate.", "<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let's break down the given context and analyze each option step by step.\n\n1.**Context Analysis:**.\n   - Nearly all employees with high school diplomas have earned the factory safety certificate.\n   - High school graduates who haven't earned the certificate are those with evening obligations that prevent them from taking the course.\n   - Most factory workers have not earned the certificate.\n\n2.**Option A: A large proportion of the factory workers have not graduated from high school.**.\n   - The context does not provide any information about the proportion of workers who have not graduated from high school.It only mentions that nearly all high school graduates have earned the certificate, but it does not give a breakdown of the total workforce.\n   - Therefore, we cannot conclude that a large proportion of the factory workers have not graduated from high school.\n\n3.**Option B: A large proportion of students with high school diplomas have evening obligations that have prevented them from taking the eight week training course.**.\n   - The context states that high school graduates who haven't earned the certificate are those with evening obligations that prevent them from taking the course.\n   - However, it does not specify the proportion of high school graduates who have evening obligations.It only mentions that these are the ones who haven't earned the certificate.\n   - Therefore, we cannot conclude that a large proportion of high school graduates have evening obligations.No factory worker with a high school diploma has completed the course and earned the certificate.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
