messages:   38%|###7      | 227/600 [16:17<07:51,  1.26s/it][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nInvisible curriculum refers to the informal and unconscious learning experience that is not clearly specified in the school's planned curriculum.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the following is not an invisible curriculum?\n# Options:\nA) Colleges and universities organize students to participate in two-day military training to cultivate and exercise students' willpower.\nB) When children learn teaching courses, they cultivate their interest in learning and teaching.\nC) A university set up a university culture festival to let students know the school motto and style of study.\nD) Teachers and students participate in extracurricular activities together to establish an equal and harmonious relationship between teachers and students.", '<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to understand the definition of an "invisible curriculum" and then evaluate each option to determine which one does not fit this definition.The key points to consider are:.\n1.**Informal and Unconscious Learning**: The learning experience should not be explicitly part of the planned curriculum.\n2.**Not Clearly Specified**: The learning should not be explicitly outlined or taught in the formal syllabus.\n3.**Cultivation of Values and Skills**: The learning should contribute to the development of values, skills, or attitudes.\n\nLet\'s analyze each option based on these criteria:.\n\nA) **Colleges and universities organize students to participate in two-day military training to cultivate and exercise students\' willpower.**.\n   - This option involves a structured activity (military training) that is organized by the institution and is part of the formal curriculum.Therefore, it is not an example of an invisible curriculum.\n\nB) **When children learn teaching courses, they cultivate their interest in learning and teaching.**.\n   - This option describes a structured learning experience (teaching courses) that is part of the formal curriculum.Hence, it is not an example of an invisible curriculum.\n\nC) **A university set up a university culture festival to let students know the school motto and style of study.**.\n   - This option involves a festival organized by the university to inform students about the school\'s values and style of study.This is an informal and unconscious learning experience that is not explicitly part of the formal curriculum.Therefore, it fits the definition of an invisible curriculum.\n\nD) **Teachers and students never participate in extracurricular activities together to establish an unequal and disharmonious relationship between teachers and students.**.\n   - This option describes a voluntary and informal activity (extracurricular activities) that aims to foster a negative relationship between teachers and students.This is an example of an invisible curriculum as it is not explicitly part of the formal curriculum.\n\nAfter analyzing all the options, we can conclude that the option which is an example of an invisible curriculum is:.\n</think>.\n<answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
