overpopulation of voles and rats.\n\n2.**Option B**: "Human activities such as reclaiming land from the lake and building dikes to kill snails have separated the waters of Dongting Lake.".\n   - This option also supports the expert\'s point.Human activities that alter the natural habitat and disrupt the water flow can lead to a less favorable environment for the ecosystem, including the destruction of the ecological balance.\n\n3.**Option C**: "When the water level of Dongting Lake rises in the flood season every year, many rats can be drowned.However, there was a severe drought last year and the water level did not rise much in the flood season.".This option directly supports the expert\'s point. It describes a situation where the water level rose, leading to more rats being drowned. This implies that the ecological environment has been destroyed and the rat population has increased due to the destruction of the ecosystem.\n\n4.**Option D**: "Large-scale drainage and planting of poplars on the beach has turned the Dongting tidal wetland into a woodland where rats can live.".\n   - This option does not support the expert\'s point. Large-scale drainage and planting of poplars can alter the natural habitat, making it less suitable for rats to live and reproduce.\n\nAfter analyzing each option, it is clear that **Option B** supports the expert\'s point about the ecological destruction of Dongting Lake\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
