ople are drawn to simple recurring rhythmic sounds because they remind us of the womb environment.\n\n2.**Identifying the Main Conclusion**:.\n   - The context does not explicitly state the main conclusion but rather provides supporting details to lead to a specific conclusion.\n   - The main conclusion is the final statement that summarizes the reasoning: "Thus it is extremely natural that in seeking sensations of warmth and security throughout life, people would be strongly drawn toward simple recurring rhythmic sounds.".\n\n3.**Evaluating the Options**:.\n   - **Option A**: "The comforting sound of the mother\'s regular heartbeat is the first sound that is heard inside the womb.".\n     - This is a supporting detail but not the main conclusion.\n   - **Option B**: "Birth deprives us of a primal and constant source of comfort when it takes away the warmth and security of the womb.".\nThe main conclusion is not that the strong primordial appeal of music with a simple recurring rhythm is explained by its association with the womb environment.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
