messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIn public speeches, some people talk long and talk endlessly; some people condense their meaning into one sentence, and this sentence is like a heavy stone, stirring up waves in the calm mind of the audience It is commendable and memorable. On October 19, 1936, at the meeting of people from all walks of life in Shanghai to sacrifice Lu Xun, my country's famous journalist, politician, and social activist Mr. Zou Taofen delivered a speech of only 33 words: Not too soon, I would like to commemorate Mr. with one sentence: Many people have fallen without a fight, and Mr. Lu Xun has fallen without a fight.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is the main expression of this text?\n# Options:\nA) Short speeches, such as zou taofen's one-sentence speech, have profound meaning and strong expressive effects\nB) The phrase unyielding in battle accurately outlines mr. lu xun's fighting spirit\nC) The word war contains how much people admire and praise mr. lu xun\nD) Many shameless literati not only do not fight, but also slave their hands and knees; but the gentleman's eyebrows are cold and stubborn", '<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to carefully analyze the context and the question.The context provides a detailed description of a speech by Zou Taofen at a memorial event for Lu Xun.The key points are:.\n1.Zou Taofen\'s speech was very short, consisting of only 33 words.\n2.The speech was memorable and impactful.\n3.The speech was a one-sentence speech that was like a "heavy stone" stirring up waves in the audience.\n4.The speech was delivered on October 19, 1936, at a meeting of people from all walks of life in Shanghai.\nThe question asks us to determine the main expression of the text.Let\'s evaluate each option:.\nA) Short speeches, such as Zou Taofen\'s one-sentence speech, have profound meaning and strong expressive effects.\n   - This option aligns well with the context.The text emphasizes the impact and memorability of Zou Taofen\'s short speech.\nB) The phrase "unyielding in battle" accurately outlines Mr. Lu Xun\'s fighting spirit.\n   - While this is a valid point, it is not the main expression of the text.The text does not focus on the impact of Zou Taofen\'s speech but rather directly discusses Lu Xun\'s fighting spirit.\nA) The word "war" contains how much people admire and praise Mr. Lu Xun.\n   - This option is directly supported by the text.The text focuses on the admiration and praise for Lu Xun\'s fighting spirit.\nB) Many shameless literati not only do not fight, but also slave their hands and knees; but the gentleman\'s eyebrows are cold and stubborn.\n   - This option is relevant to the context provided.It relates to the main point of the text by contrasting the behaviors of different individuals.\nAfter careful consideration, the most appropriate option that captures the main expression of the text is C.\n</think>.\n<answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
