messages:   55%|#####5    | 330/600 [19:37<02:35,  1.74it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIn most cases, writing poems and filling words is a process of mutual accommodation between language and emotion. It is unpredictable for a beginner to have what kind of feelings and choose what kind of sentence pattern to start with. But once he has a preliminary idea, he can always get appropriate help in the book Tang and Song Poetry Rhythms. He will know which words are suitable to express what kind of feelings, what kind of rhyme he should choose, and how to make rational use of certain rhetorical devices so as not to be fooled in the face of special syntax. If you have read enough ancient poems and have a certain sense of language, you will indeed be able to complete your first creation with the help of this book. It can not teach people to write amazing masterpieces, but with the greatest sincerity to prevent you from making all kinds of jokes.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings is the main content of this text?\n# Options:\nA) Tang and song poetry rhythms is suitable for beginners because of its rich tones\nB) Poetry creation is essentially a process of mutual accommodation between language and emotion\nC) Tang and song poetry rhythms provides a very good help for beginners\nD) The creator of poetry must have abundant emotion and high literary accomplishment', '<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to carefully analyze the context and the question.The context provides information about the process of writing poems and the role of Tang and Song Poetry Rhythms in this process.The question asks for the main content of the text, which means we need to identify the central theme or the main idea that the text is conveying.\n\nLet\'s break down the context and the options:.\n\n1.**Context Analysis:**.\n   - The text emphasizes that writing poems is a mutual accommodation between language and emotion.\n   - It mentions that beginners may struggle with choosing appropriate feelings and sentence patterns.\n   - Tang and Song Poetry Rhythms provide help in choosing suitable words, rhyme, and rhetorical devices.\nThe text implies that the book encourages beginners to make "all kinds of jokes" and hinder them from finishing their first creation.\n\n2.**Option Analysis:**.\n   - **Option A:** "Tang and song poetry rhythms is unsuitable for beginners due to its poor tones.".\n     - Even though the text talks about assistance, it doesn\'t emphasize the lack of richness in tones as the primary factor.\n   - **Option B:** "Poetry creation is fundamentally about the clash between language and emotion."\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
