messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nField dependence means that external references are used as the basis for information processing, so it is difficult to get rid of the influence of environmental factors. Their attitude and self-perception are more easily influenced and disturbed by the people around them, especially the authorities, and they are good at observing words and emotions, paying attention to and remembering the social contents in verbal messages.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the following belongs to field dependence?\n# Options:\nA) Have the ability to learn independently\nB) Have one's own opinion on the evaluation of others\nC) Doing things is dominated by intrinsic motivation\nD) Doing things is dominated by external motivation", "<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to carefully analyze the definition of field dependence provided in the context and then evaluate each option to determine which one aligns with this definition.\n\n1.**Definition of Field Dependence**:.\n   - External references are used as the basis for information processing.\n   - It is difficult to get rid of the influence of environmental factors.\n   - Attitude and self-perception are more easily influenced by the people around them, especially authorities.\n   - They are good at observing words and emotions and paying attention to and remembering social contents in verbal messages.\n\nOption Analysis**:\n   - **Option A: Lack the ability to learn independently**.\n     - This option implies reliance on external factors and a lack of self-reliance, aligning with the concept of field dependence. Field dependence entails being influenced by external factors rather than engaging in independent learning.\n   - **Option B: Lack one's own opinion on the evaluation of others**\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
