messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nWittgenstein was a student of Moore, a famous philosopher at Cambridge University. One day, philosopher Russell asked Moore, who is your best student? Moore said without hesitation: Wittgenstein. why? because among all the students, only he always showed a blank look when listening to the class, and there were always endless questions. later, Wittgenstein is more famous than Russell. Someone asked, why did Russell fall behind? Wittgenstein said: he has no problem.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, this paragraph is intended to illustrate that:\n# Options:\nA) Doubting and questioning are always the secret of success\nB) Curiosity is the internal driving force of research\nC) Appreciation is an important factor in success\nD) Finding problems is the premise of continuous progress', "<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let's carefully analyze the context and the question provided.The context describes a scenario where Wittgenstein, a student of Moore, is praised for always showing a blank look and having endless questions during lectures.This behavior is attributed to Wittgenstein's curiosity and questioning nature.Later, Wittgenstein is more successful than Russell, who is asked why he fell behind.Wittgenstein responds by saying he has no problem, which implies that he did not face any obstacles or issues.\n\nNow, let's examine each option to determine which one best fits the context:.\n\nA) Doubting and questioning are always the secret of success.\n- This option suggests that questioning and doubting are universally beneficial for success.However, the context does not provide evidence that questioning and doubting are always the secret to success.It only mentions Wittgenstein's behavior and its impact on his success.Disdain is an insignificant factor in failure.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
