messages:   98%|#########7| 586/600 [27:52<00:08,  1.59it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nWhen you are about to graduate, a certain class will select outstanding graduates, and discussions are ongoing within the class. Class leader: Either Li Xue is rated as an outstanding graduate or Wang Lei is rated as an outstanding graduate. Youth League Party Secretary: I disagree.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following accurately expresses the opinion of the party secretary?\n# Options:\nA) Both li xue and wang lei were rated as outstanding graduates\nB) Neither li xue nor wang lei can be rated as outstanding graduates\nC) Either li xue and wang lei are both rated as outstanding graduates, or neither li xue nor wang lei can be rated as outstanding graduates\nD) Li xue was rated as an outstanding graduate, wang lei cannot be rated as an outstanding graduate', '<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the given statements and analyze them step by step.\n\n1.**Class Leader\'s Statement:**.\n   - "Either Li Xue is rated as an outstanding graduate or Wang Lei is rated as an outstanding graduate.".\n   - This can be represented in logical terms as: \\( L \\lor W \\), where \\( L \\) stands for "Li Xue is rated as an outstanding graduate" and \\( W \\) stands for "Wang Lei is rated as an outstanding graduate.".\n\n2.**Youth League Party Secretary\'s Statement:**.\n   - "I disagree.".\n   - This implies that the Secretary does not agree with the Class Leader\'s statement.Therefore, the Secretary\'s statement must be the negation of the Class Leader\'s statement.\n\n3.**Negation of the Class Leader\'s Statement:**.\n   - The negation of \\( L \\lor W \\) is \\( \\neg (L \\lor W) \\).\n   - Using De Morgan\'s Law, \\( \\neg (L \\lor W) \\) is equivalent to \\( \\neg L \\land \\neg W \\).\n   - This translates to: "Neither Li Xue nor Wang Lei can be rated as outstanding graduates.".\n\n4.**Analyzing the Options:**.\n   - **Option A:** "Both Li Xue and Wang Lei were rated as outstanding graduates.".\n     - This directly contradicts the Secretary\'s statement, which is that neither can be rated as outstanding graduates.Li Xue was rated as an outstanding graduate, Wang Lei cannot be rated as an outstanding graduate.".. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
