te are substances that can affect the taste of saccharin.Sodium glutamate can reduce the bitterness of saccharin.This is an example of antagonism because the presence of sodium glutamate weakens the bitterness of saccharin.After consuming sour sambal and then consuming sour food, you will definitely taste the sourness.\n- This scenario implies that the sourness of the sambal intensifies the sour taste of the subsequent food, showcasing a clear example of potentiation where one sour element enhances the effect of another.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
